<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE-Interleisure raises yr shr, div drops.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Interleisure raises yr shr, div drops.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre-excepts	   31.6	  vs  27.2</p>
<p>    - attrib		  41.5	  vs  26.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  6.75	 vs  12.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   78.77	 vs 50.07</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   96.69	 vs 75.90</p>
<p>    Tax			 20.73	 vs 25.53</p>
<p>    Interest received     3.30	  vs 0.74 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  482.20	vs 462.47</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     18.83 gain  vs 1.64 loss</p>
<p>Full name: Interleisure Ltd (Beverages, hotels &amp; leisure)</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm is unbundling its assets after agreeing to sell the majority of its businesses to Primedia Ltd and therefore is not paying a final dividend.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
